{
  "name": "23-owner-housekeeping",
  "description": "The owner creates a project, changes its brief while a builder holds a task, changes which task is claimed and how long its lease lasts, then deletes task and project content.",
  "covers": [
    "PRD The briefing and agent interface, AP-27. Editing the whole brief replaces one entry and keeps the other. A holder must acknowledge the changed briefing before working.",
    "PRD Behaviour every client can rely on, AP-28. Raising the newer task to high priority makes it claimable ahead of the older normal-priority task.",
    "PRD Timers and leases, AP-39. The changed lease length applies to the next grant.",
    "PRD Quality requirements, AP-36. Delete content of a Done task, refuse a project with an open task, then delete the project and the remaining task content without changing steps."
  ],
